{
  "dom_id": "step-165335",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Multiplying Polynomials",
  "problem": "Simplify $-3t^3\\left(3t^2+2t\\right).$",
  "worked_solution": "We multiply each term inside the parentheses by the term outside the parentheses, simplify using the rules of exponents, and then we add the results together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{t}^{3}(3{t}^{2}+2t) & = \\\\ (-3{t}^{3})\\cdot (3{t}^{2})+(-3{t}^{3})\\cdot (2t) & = \\\\ ((-3)\\cdot 3)({t}^{3}\\cdot {t}^{2})+((-3)\\cdot 2)({t}^{3}\\cdot t) & = \\\\ (-9)({t}^{3+2})+(-6)({t}^{3+1}) & = \\\\ (-9)({t}^{5})+(-6)({t}^{4}) & = \\\\ -9{t}^{5}-6{t}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
